0104-venus-gpu-surfaces: the GPU side of SweetSurface and SweetFramebuffer (topaz merge)

Merged from Topaz's 0901, 0924, 0932, 0937, 0939, 0940, 0942, 0943, 0946, 0948 and 0949 (the
SweetSurface and SweetFramebuffer parts), onto our 0046-0101 chain. Topaz's 0945 reorder of the
vsync payload is NOT taken: ours stays (count, time, 0, 0).

Every GPU behaviour is behind the boot-arg sweetgpukeep=1, read once (sweet_gpu_keep() in
SweetSurface.cpp, declared in SweetSurface.h). Without it the surfaces and the framebuffer behave
as before this patch:
  - SweetSurface::free(): the reserve is given back only with the gate on.
  - sweet_gpu_pool_eligible(): false without the gate (GPU pool surfaces).
  - SweetSurface create: the contiguous reserve and the physically contiguous path only with the
    gate; otherwise the plain inTaskWithOptions allocation, as before.
  - AppleCLCD::start(): RedwoodWaitsForGPU property and publishModes() (TimingElements /
    ColorElements, 60 Hz) only with the gate.
  - AppleCLCD::present(): topaz_surface_drawn() only with the gate.
  - externalMethod selector 79 (kSweetFBGetBlock): only with the gate; without it the selector
    takes the default path as before.
  - sweetfps=1 (SWEET FPS line, topaz 0946) keeps its own boot-arg and is not a GPU gate.

Header: SweetSurface.h defines SWEET_TOPAZ_GPU 1 (so the GPU code is compiled) and adds the
fields RedwoodGPU.cpp reads: drawn, gpuPool, scanoutPhys, poolSize, wrapped (false), wrapDelta
(0), scanoutSlot (-1).

Not ported: topaz 0901 topaz_adreno_init (venus GPU bring-up is venus_adreno.c), 0092/0099/0100
scanout and hold structures, 0933/0944/0945 direct presenter, 0941 vsync follow.

